# Lesson 11: English Vocabulary - Idioms and Phrases

## Core Idioms Master List

| Idiom | Meaning | Hindi Translation |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **At the drop of a hat** | Immediately / Without delay | तुरंत |
| **At sixes and sevens** | In disorder / Confused | अव्यवस्थित क्रम |
| **A blessing in disguise** | Something good that seemed bad at first | छिपा हुआ वरदान |
| **At sea** | Surprised / Confused / Bewildered | भौचक्का / भ्रमित |
| **Apple of discord** | Matter of dispute / Cause of quarrel | झगड़े की जड़ |
| **A square peg in a round hole** | A person unfit for a position | अनुपयुक्त व्यक्ति |
| **An axe to grind** | A private / selfish reason to do something | निजी स्वार्थ छिपा होना |
| **Apple of one's eye** | Very precious / Dear | आँखों का तारा |
| **A wild goose chase** | A useless / pointless search | निरर्थक प्रयास |
| **A live wire** | Lively and active person | फुर्तीला व्यक्ति |
| **At a stone's throw** | At a very short distance | बहुत नजदीक |
| **A bolt from the blue** | A sudden unexpected event/shock | अचानक आई मुसीबत |
| **A dark horse** | An unexpected winner / Hidden talent | छुपारुस्तम |
| **A man of letters** | Scholar / Wise man | विद्वान व्यक्ति |
| **Break a leg** | Good luck / Express support | शुभकामना देना |
| **Break the ice** | Break silence / Start conversation | चुप्पी तोड़ना |
| **Bite the bullet** | Face a difficult situation brave | खतरे/मुसीबत का सामना करना |
| **Beat around the bush** | Avoid talking about the main topic | घुमा-फिराकर बात करना |
| **Burn the midnight oil** | Work/study late into the night | देर रात तक मेहनत करना |
| **Bury the hatchet** | Make peace / End hostility | पुरानी दुश्मनी भूलना |
| **By leaps and bounds** | Rapidly / Very fast | दिन-दूनी रात-चौगुनी |
| **Cut a sorry figure** | Make a poor impression | निराशाजनक प्रदर्शन करना |
| **Cry over spilt milk** | Regret about past unchangeable loss | व्यर्थ में पछताना |
| **Die in harness** | Die while still in service | कार्यकाल के दौरान मृत्यु होना |
| **Face the music** | Bear the negative consequences | परिणाम भुगतना |
| **Feather one's own nest** | Provide for oneself dishonestly | अपना स्वार्थ साधना |
